@startuml
title Variant A — Push timeout, SMS provider failover, late ACK
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant "Scheduler / Orchestrator\n+ outbox relay" as O
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "RabbitMQ" as Q
participant "SMS Adapter" as A
participant "SMS-A" as PA
participant "SMS-B" as PB
participant "Receipt API" as R
participant "Mobile app" as App

note over O,App : Existing notification; push was accepted, no app ACK.
O -> DB : At t0 + 2 s: lock due notification
alt Already CONFIRMED
  DB --> O : No work; skip failover
else No confirmation
  O -> DB : Commit next generation, SMS-A attempt + outbox
  O -> Q : Publish SMS-A attempt; wait for confirm
  Q --> O : Confirm
  Q -> A : Attempt ID
  A -> DB : Check state; claim attempt; commit
  A -> PA : Send SMS (target <= t0 + 3 s)
  PA --> A : Definitive rejection, not accepted
  A -> DB : Commit FAILED + outcome outbox
  A -> Q : ACK
  O -> DB : Lock state; commit SMS-B attempt + outbox
  O -> Q : Publish SMS-B attempt; wait for confirm
  Q --> O : Confirm
  Q -> A : SMS-B attempt ID
  A -> DB : Claim B after checking no confirmation
  A -> PB : Send with stable attempt_id
  PB --> A : Accepted + provider_message_id
  A -> DB : Commit WAITING_RECEIPT
  A -> Q : ACK
  PB -> R : Signed delivered DLR
  R -> DB : Commit receipt + outbox
  R --> PB : 200
  O -> DB : Process receipt; commit CONFIRMED
end
App -> R : Late push ACK
R -> DB : Persist duplicate-channel evidence + outbox
R --> App : 200
O -> DB : Keep CONFIRMED; no email or new attempts
note over O,App : If an ACK wins the DB lock before the next claim,
note over O,App : the next send is suppressed. An already permitted SMS cannot be recalled.
@enduml
